# DB2 DBA Health Checklist
# Format: [TYPE] CHECK_ID | Risk | Description | Expected
# TYPE: AUTO = script can verify, MANUAL = requires DBA eyes on it
# Risk: HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW
# This file is parsed by db2_dba_checker.sh — do not alter the pipe-delimited structure of checklist lines

---

## SECTION: Log Configuration

[AUTO]   LOG001 | HIGH   | LOGFILSIZ is 65536 (256MB) — optimal for HADR NEARSYNC                      | 65536
[AUTO]   LOG002 | HIGH   | LOGPRIMARY >= 50 (~12GB primary log space)                                   | 50
[AUTO]   LOG003 | HIGH   | LOGSECOND >= 600 (~150GB secondary — covers worst case REORG log burst)      | 600
[AUTO]   LOG004 | MEDIUM | LOGBUFSZ >= 65536 (256MB in-memory log buffer)                              | 65536
[AUTO]   LOG005 | HIGH   | LOGARCHCOMPR1 is ON (50-70% NAS space reduction)                            | ON
[AUTO]   LOG006 | HIGH   | LOGARCHMETH1 is configured (not blank or LOGRETAIN)                         | CONFIGURED
[AUTO]   LOG007 | MEDIUM | LOGARCHMETH2 is configured (dual destination — NAS fallback)                | CONFIGURED
[MANUAL] LOG008 | HIGH   | NAS archive mount is dedicated to DB2 — not shared with other workloads     | VERIFIED
[MANUAL] LOG009 | HIGH   | NFS mount options set: hard mount, appropriate timeo and retrans values     | VERIFIED
[MANUAL] LOG010 | MEDIUM | NAS filesystem utilisation is below 70%                                     | VERIFIED

---

## SECTION: Recovery History and Retention

[AUTO]   REC001 | HIGH   | AUTO_DEL_REC_OBJ is ON (physical archive logs cleaned with history prune)  | ON
[AUTO]   REC002 | MEDIUM | REC_HIS_RETENTN is 35 days (aligned to backup retention + buffer)           | 35
[AUTO]   REC003 | MEDIUM | NUM_DB_BACKUPS >= 3 (minimum recovery chains retained)                      | 3
[AUTO]   REC004 | MEDIUM | Recovery history contains at least one FULL backup in the last 7 days       | PRESENT
[AUTO]   REC005 | HIGH   | No backup failures in recovery history in last 7 days                       | NONE

---

## SECTION: HADR Health

[AUTO]   HADR001 | HIGH   | HADR_STATE is PEER                                                        | PEER
[AUTO]   HADR002 | HIGH   | HADR_SYNCMODE is NEARSYNC                                                 | NEARSYNC
[AUTO]   HADR003 | HIGH   | HADR_CONNECT_STATUS is CONNECTED                                          | CONNECTED
[AUTO]   HADR004 | HIGH   | HADR_LOG_GAP is below 500MB                                               | <500MB
[AUTO]   HADR005 | MEDIUM | HADR_PEER_WINDOW_END is set (not null — peer window is configured)         | SET
[MANUAL] HADR006 | HIGH   | Network latency between primary and standby is acceptable for NEARSYNC    | VERIFIED
[MANUAL] HADR007 | MEDIUM | Standby server has adequate disk for log replay accumulation              | VERIFIED
[MANUAL] HADR008 | HIGH   | HADR failover has been tested in the last 6 months                        | VERIFIED

---

## SECTION: Archive Log Storage (HCP / S3)

[AUTO]   ARC001 | HIGH   | LOGARCHMETH1 is set to S3 (HCP object storage preferred over NFS)         | S3
[MANUAL] ARC002 | HIGH   | HCP S3 endpoint is reachable from the DB2 server                          | VERIFIED
[MANUAL] ARC003 | HIGH   | GSKit keystore exists at expected path on DB2 server                      | VERIFIED
[MANUAL] ARC004 | HIGH   | mTLS client certificate is valid and not expiring within 60 days          | VERIFIED
[MANUAL] ARC005 | HIGH   | HCP server certificate CN/SAN matches DB2_S3_ENDPOINT hostname exactly    | VERIFIED
[MANUAL] ARC006 | HIGH   | HCP tenant is configured to require client certificates (mTLS enforced)   | VERIFIED
[MANUAL] ARC007 | MEDIUM | HCP lifecycle policy is set to 45-50 days on the archive log bucket       | VERIFIED
[MANUAL] ARC008 | MEDIUM | Certificate rotation runbook is documented and calendar reminder is set   | VERIFIED
[MANUAL] ARC009 | MEDIUM | DB2_S3_SSL_SERVER_VERIFY is TRUE in db2set output                        | VERIFIED

---

## SECTION: REORG Readiness

[AUTO]   REO001 | HIGH   | Current log space utilisation is below 60% (headroom for REORG burst)     | <60%
[AUTO]   REO002 | HIGH   | HADR_STATE is PEER — do not REORG if standby is not in peer state         | PEER
[AUTO]   REO003 | HIGH   | Secondary log space is not currently being consumed (LOGSECOND at rest)   | 0
[AUTO]   REO004 | MEDIUM | Indexes with CLUSTERRATIO below 80 — candidates for REORG                 | IDENTIFIED
[AUTO]   REO005 | MEDIUM | Indexes with NLEVELS above 4 — may indicate excessive fragmentation        | IDENTIFIED
[AUTO]   REO006 | LOW    | Indexes unused for 90+ days — candidates for review/drop                  | IDENTIFIED
[AUTO]   REO007 | MEDIUM | Table free page percentage — tables with >20% free pages need REORG       | IDENTIFIED
[MANUAL] REO008 | HIGH   | Full database backup completed before any offline REORG                   | VERIFIED
[MANUAL] REO009 | HIGH   | Maintenance window is confirmed and communicated                          | VERIFIED
[MANUAL] REO010 | HIGH   | LOGSECOND 600 verified as adequate before offline REORG on 70GB indexes   | VERIFIED
[MANUAL] REO011 | MEDIUM | Online REORG preferred over offline unless deep maintenance window exists  | VERIFIED
[MANUAL] REO012 | MEDIUM | Index REORGs to be staggered — not all 70GB rebuilt simultaneously        | VERIFIED

---

## SECTION: Index Health

[AUTO]   IDX001 | MEDIUM | Index to table size ratio — 70GB indexes / 30GB table data flagged        | REVIEWED
[AUTO]   IDX002 | LOW    | Indexes unused for 90+ days listed for DBA review                         | LISTED
[AUTO]   IDX003 | MEDIUM | Indexes with NLEVELS > 4 listed (excessive B-tree depth = fragmentation)  | LISTED

